<div class="options-page">
<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Mike Trounce</a>

<h1>Consultant</h1>
<p class="intro">
Sometimes you just want someone who's done this before to look at what you've got and tell you straight what's wrong with it — before anyone spends a penny fixing anything.
</p>

<section class="content-section">
<h2>What this looks like</h2>
<p>
We talk — about your dealflow, say: where your leads actually come from, where they drop off, what's slow, what's working better than you think. I tell you what I'd change and why. No build, no deliverable, nothing installed — just the conversation and the thinking behind it.
</p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
<h2>If it turns into work</h2>
<p>
Most of what gets built for clients starts as exactly this kind of conversation. If something we talk through is worth actually doing — a CRM, a website, a marketing push — that's the <a href="/builder">Builder</a> side of things.
</p>
</section>
